WEBVTT

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:04.646
A standard full-time day in the US is 8 hours.

00:00:04.646 --> 00:00:06.869
A standard full-time week is 40.

00:00:08.219 --> 00:00:14.181
Anything you work above either of those thresholds, by day or by week, counts as overtime.

00:00:14.181 --> 00:00:17.029
Cisco applies this approach in every state.

00:00:18.379 --> 00:00:25.867
Overtime is paid at 1.5 times your regular rate, for every hour over 8 in a day, or over 40 in a week.

00:00:27.217 --> 00:00:32.358
Hours worked on a Cisco-observed US holiday also qualify as overtime.

00:00:32.358 --> 00:00:37.052
Workday recognizes holidays, so just enter your hours as usual.

00:00:38.402 --> 00:00:43.181
And once you go past 12 hours in a single day, the rate rises to double time.

00:00:44.531 --> 00:00:52.147
Always get your manager's approval before you work overtime, and record every hour in Workday, whether it was pre-approved or not.
